00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Reservoir Dogs is a 1992 American independent heist film written and directed
by Quentin Tarantino in his feature-length directorial debut.

16
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
It stars Harvey Keitel, Tim Roth, Chris Penn, Steve Buscemi, Lawrence Tierney, Michael Madsen, Tarantino,
and Edward Bunker as diamond thieves whose heist of a jewelry store goes terribly wrong.

17
01:02:20,000 --> 01:02:26,000
Kirk Baltz, Randy Brooks, and Steven Wright also play supporting roles.

18
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
The film incorporates many motifs that have become Tarantino's hallmarks: violent
crime, pop culture references, profanity, and nonlinear storytelling.

19
01:09:40,000 --> 01:09:46,000
The film is regarded as a classic independent film and a cult film.

20
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
Although controversial at first for its depictions of violence and heavy use of profanity,
Reservoir Dogs was generally well received, and the cast was praised by many critics.

21
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
Despite not being heavily promoted during its theatrical run, the film became a modest
success in the United States after grossing $2.9 million against its scant budget.

22
01:20:40,000 --> 01:20:46,000
It achieved higher popularity after the success of
Tarantino's next film, Pulp Fiction (1994).

23
01:24:20,000 --> 01:24:26,000
A soundtrack was released featuring songs used in the
film, which are mostly from the 1970s.

24
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
It was named "Greatest Independent Film of All Time" by the British film magazine
Empire, which in 2008 also named it the 97th-greatest film ever made.

25
01:31:40,000 --> 01:31:46,000
The film explores themes of escape, jewelry, psychopath, traitor, ear.

